Fraunces — bundled display font (OFL 1.1)
==========================================

Files in this folder
- Fraunces-SemiBold.ttf — PostScript name "Fraunces-SemiBold", weight 600.
  Used by Theme.Font display roles (Tokens.swift checks exactly this name).
- Fraunces-Regular.ttf — PostScript name "Fraunces-Regular", weight 400.
  Bundled for future body-serif use; no code references it yet.
- OFL.txt — verbatim SIL Open Font License 1.1 (also embedded in each
  font's name table, ID 13).

Source (preferred source, OFL)
- https://github.com/google/fonts/tree/main/ofl/fraunces
- Variable font: ofl/fraunces/Fraunces[SOFT,WONK,opsz,wght].ttf
  (downloaded 2026-11-05; 360,440 bytes)
- License: ofl/fraunces/OFL.txt (copied here verbatim)
- Upstream project: https://github.com/undercasetype/Fraunces

How the static files were produced
- google/fonts ships Fraunces ONLY as a variable font; there is no static
  SemiBold/Regular file in the repo (no static/ directory).
- The variable font's own named instances resolve to PostScript names like
  "Fraunces_600wght", NOT "Fraunces-SemiBold", so the variable file was NOT
  bundled as-is — Tokens.swift looks up "Fraunces-SemiBold" and would not
  find it.
- Each static file was pinned from the variable font at that instance's own
  coordinates (fontTools varLib.instancer):
  SemiBold: wght=600 opsz=9 SOFT=0 WONK=1; Regular: wght=400 opsz=9 SOFT=0
  WONK=1. The instancer left stale default names ("Fraunces-9ptBlack"), so
  the name table was corrected to the instance's canonical names
  (family "Fraunces", subfamily "SemiBold"/"Regular", PostScript names
  "Fraunces-SemiBold"/"Fraunces-Regular", OS/2 weight 600/400, no bold or
  italic flags). Verified with fc-scan and fontTools after the fix.
- This is a permitted OFL modification (instancing + name correction); the
  OFL text and copyright notice are preserved in OFL.txt and in each file.

Registration
- src/ios/Info.plist: UIAppFonts lists both files.
- src/ios/Minis.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj: both files are in the Minis
  target's Resources phase (Fonts group, FNT000* IDs). The license note and
  OFL.txt are deliberately NOT in the target — they are not app resources.
